    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d918">

                <pb facs="1082" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg986"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 762.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received and communicated to the
                    Secretary of the Navy your telegram of the 21st instant, which deciphered reads
                    as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>British Government has made inquiry and is convinced there is no truth in
                            report of Spanish privateer at Vancouver.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
